      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T19:21:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if this fails, we should have a retry count to try again before ultimately abandoning the commit with an error message. This should allow for busy I2C buses and not let failed writes fall silently through the cracks.",
      "revId": "cb308f398e3431045df66262ffef645754835ab7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d8181656_fe394c63",
        "filename": "dbus-sdr/storagecommands.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002827
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T05:26:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. writeFruCache() now checks the return value and retries up to 3\ntimes at 2s intervals, logging each attempt, then abandons with an error\nnaming devId/bus/addr/size. The counter lives in the per-device context and\nresets on a new session.Retry goes through the timer rather than an inline loop, since writeFru()\nis a blocking call and ipmid is single-threaded.Note: the write timer is now a boost::asio::steady_timer. Re-arming\nan sdbusplus::Timer from inside its own callback did not work,\ntimeoutHandler() disables the event source after userCallBack()\nreturns, so only one retry ever fired. Since the flush no longer runs\ninside that dispatch, it can also erase the context outright rather than\nclearing the buffer and leaving a hollow entry behind. The active flag went with it, since it existed only to mark such an entry. So the previous use-after-free caveat no longer applies.",
      "parentUuid": "d8fcd5cd_047dd78e",
      "revId": "cb308f398e3431045df66262ffef645754835ab7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7e61c3d_615836d2",
        "filename": "dbus-sdr/storagecommands.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 340,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T19:21:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "check the response of writeFru so we don\u0027t drop failed writes.\n```\nif (writeFru(wctx.bus, wctx.addr, wctx.data))\n{\n    it \u003d fruWriteCtxMap.erase(it);\n}\nelse\n{\n    ++it;\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 339,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 340,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "cb308f398e3431045df66262ffef645754835ab7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
